# Reviewing changes in `orchestration/`

The unified reviewer (`prompts/codeReviewer/v3/`) loads **`orchestration/REVIEW.md`**
for any changed path under `orchestration/`. That map cites rule IDs from
`orchestration/AGENTS.md` (e.g. `AP-5`, the new-graph-node `⚠️ Ask first` → ADR trigger)
and root `AGENTS.md` (`Invariant #8`) — it never restates the rule text.

Deterministic checks that fire here first (precedence over LLM):
- D1 dependency table (`check_dependency_rules`) — orchestration is the only layer that
  may import `langgraph`/`langchain`; nodes delegate logic to `components/` + `services/`.
- D2 ADR.1 (`detect_adr1_missing`) — a new node in `orchestration/react_loop.py` with no
  new `docs/adr/` file in the same diff is flagged (use `--from-git-diff`).
- D5 AP-5 — nodes must be thin wrappers (≤10–15 lines); domain logic belongs in
  `components/` (LLM-judged).

Dispatch the reviewer:

```bash
python -m meta.code_reviewer --from-git-diff --git-base HEAD --prompt-version v3 --output review.json
```

Deterministic findings are the gate; the v3 LLM judge is WI-8 certified (TPR/TNR = 1.0) so LLM verdicts are gate-grade for the routed LLM-only rules — re-record when the judge model changes.
Full contract: `docs/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`.
